DESK-MEASURED DIAGNOSIS (verified today, do not re-derive):
1. VM egress is a fake-IP transparent gateway plus an HTTP proxy at hatch-egress-proxy:3128 (198.19.0.1 / [fd8b:4f84:7d32:99::1]); credentials ride in the env proxy URLs (HTTPS_PROXY etc.). The proxy MITMs TLS with a private CA: trusted by the system CA store (curl/node verify fine), NOT by Chromium's root store.
2. Shell tools reach the proxy and the internet fine (curl: CONNECT 200, TLS completes for google.com/chatgpt.com/accounts.google.com). Chromium cannot use the gateway proxy directly: NetLog shows the proxy CONNECT job dying (ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED on the proxy connection; direct requests to the gateway address fail ERR_ACCESS_DENIED), surfacing as ERR_TUNNEL_CONNECTION_FAILED for EVERY site — not Gemini-specific.
3. A loopback relay works: when Chromium sends CONNECT to a relay listening on 127.0.0.1 and the relay's node process opens the upstream connection to the real proxy and forwards the CONNECT, the tunnel establishes (proxy replies 200 with or without Proxy-Authorization). TLS through the tunnel then fails ERR_CERT_AUTHORITY_INVALID (the MITM CA) — cured by ignoreHTTPSErrors.

